            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral traumatic hip dislocation associated with sacro-iliac dislocation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5301/HIP.2008.2771</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare injury in an 18-year-old woman who sustained posterior bilateral hip dislocation with sacro-iliac dislocation after a high energy motor vehicle accident. She was treated by closed reduction and skeletal traction. Bilateral traumatic hip dislocation is an uncommon occurrence. Rarer still is bilateral traumatic hip dislocation associated with sacro-iliac dislocation because it combines two different mechanisms of trauma. (Hip International 2002; 1: 47-9).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
